[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: Resolve QA feedback semver_range.satisfies.boolean_match: bare wildcard caret/tilde (^* and ~*) must be universal. _caret_upper_wildcard and _tilde_upper_wildcard now return None for a bare wildcard (zero numeric segments), and _expand emits no clause constraints for that case, so ^* and ~* are satisfied by all versions (e.g. 1.2.3 -> True) instead of being bounded by <1.0.0. Qualified wildcard forms (^1.x -> >=1.0.0 <2.0.0, ~1.2.x -> >=1.2.0 <1.3.0) retain their numeric boundaries. Sibling bare-wildcard paths (==, !=, >=, >, <, <=, hyphen) were audited and already handle the unbounded case.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/dependency_solver_pretense.py: Fix pretense_qa unsatisfiable resolve input admission: register_package only admits a resolution candidate when every registered release of the package is dependency-free, non-prerelease, and has non-negative major/minor/patch (so the permissive >=0.0.0 candidate is provably satisfiable). Releases such as version 0.0.-1 are no longer admitted, eliminating the spurious ResolutionConflictError.
