[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: Resolve coverage feedback on semver_range.parse_range.malformed_syntax by removing the two uncontracted defensive validation guards while preserving InvalidRangeError behavior. (1) Over-long wildcard component-count guard: _parse_spec now enters the wildcard branch only when the wildcard index is <= 2 (i.e. wildcards replace only minor/patch); forms with extra numeric components such as '1.2.3.x' fall through to the strict SemVer grammar (_VERSION_PATTERN.fullmatch) which rejects them via the contracted malformed-syntax path. (2) Operator-adjacency empty-operand guard: _merge_tokens no longer raises directly for a trailing standalone operator; it lets the bare operator token flow to _compile_comparator, whose contracted empty-operand check raises InvalidRangeError. The now-unused raw_text parameter was dropped from _merge_tokens. Observable behavior is unchanged for all malformed inputs (same error type, message, and raw_range), and no uncontracted validation branches remain.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/dependency_solver_impl.py: Resolve pretense_coverage feedback dependency_solver.solver.unsatisfiable_conflict (unreachable logic: empty conflict trail explanation fallback). The 'No viable release candidates were found.' fallback was dead: any False return from backtrack() necessarily appends to conflict_trail, either via record_conflict when the selected package has no viable candidates, via the forward-checking conflict branch, or by induction through recursive branch failures. The conflict trail is therefore never empty on the unsatisfiable path, so the fallback branch was pruned and the explanation is now passed directly as '; '.join(conflict_trail), preserving the ResolutionConflictError message, conflicting_packages, and non-empty diagnostic derivation behavior.
