[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_pretense.py: Expand the closed parse_range caller domain VALID_RANGE_TEXTS with contract-valid range forms required by pretense_coverage: bare-wildcard comparators and prefixes ('!=*','<*','<=*','>*','^*','~*'), zero-major caret prefixes ('^0.2.3','^0.0.3'), and minor-precision caret wildcard bands ('^1.2.x','^0.2.x'). semver_range.parse_range requires comparators, caret and tilde applied to wildcard expressions and zero-major prefix expansion, so the runtime-checked require_arg domain must admit these texts; the implementation real tests now exercise every admitted domain entry.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_impl_pretense.py: Resolve pretense_coverage gaps for bare wildcard comparator/prefix bands and zero-major caret expansion: add TestSemverRangeImplReal scenarios parsing '!=*','<*','<=*','>*','^*','~*' (every bare-wildcard comparator and prefix), '^0.2.3','^0.0.3' (zero-major caret expansion) and '^1.2.x','^0.2.x' (caret wildcard minor bands) with satisfies band checks for the zero-major and wildcard caret bands (^0.2.3 covers 0.2.3..0.2.x, excludes 0.3.0; ^0.0.3 covers only 0.0.3; ^1.2.x covers 1.2.0..1.9.9, excludes 2.0.0; ^0.2.x covers 0.2.x, excludes 0.3.0), and add malformed leading-zero wildcard-component violations '01.x' and '>=01.x' via violating(InvalidRangeError). All parse_range literals are now inside the interface-declared VALID_RANGE_TEXTS domain (expanded in semver_range_pretense.py), and every admitted domain entry is exercised by a real scenario.
